{#
calendar/_caldav_form.html.twig — connect a CalDAV server, inside the modal.

Delegates to _partials/_modal_form.html.twig for the frame, body and footer, the
way calendar/_form.html.twig does. Field order is the flow: the address, then
what to call it, then the credential and the deliberate option of reusing a
mail account's stored password — CalDavConnectType decides which fields exist
and says why they are in that order.

The form carries data-ui--modal-keep-open, and that is the only unusual thing
here. The modal closes on any successful turbo:submit-end, but a successful
connect answers with the subscribe list rather than with a stream: connecting a
server and then closing the dialog would leave the user to find the new
connection in the list behind it and press a second button for the thing they
came to do.

The "Connect my Nextcloud" shortcut renders this same form without the
address field (CalDavConnectType's `fixed_address`), and the address the
administrator set is shown as a line of text instead — read off the connection
the form is bound to, because that is the value that will be used.

Variables:
  form   FormView
  error  string|null  what the server said when the credentials were tried
#}
{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
    {% set fixed_address = form.baseUrl is defined ? null : form.vars.value.baseUrl %}

    {% embed '_partials/_modal_form.html.twig' with {
        form: form,
        title: (fixed_address is null ? 'settings.calendars.caldav.title' : 'settings.calendars.nextcloud.title')|trans,
        submit_label: 'settings.calendars.caldav.submit'|trans,
        form_attr: { 'data-ui--modal-keep-open': '' },
        error: error,
        fixed_address: fixed_address,
    } only %}
        {% block before_fields %}
            {% if fixed_address is null %}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                    {{ 'settings.calendars.caldav.intro'|trans }}
                </p>
            {% else %}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                    {{ 'settings.calendars.nextcloud.intro'|trans }}
                </p>
                <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-soft" data-nextcloud-address>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-server text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="font-mono truncate">{{ fixed_address }}</span>
                </p>
            {% endif %}

            {# The verification failure, not a validation one. The form was
               filled in correctly and the server refused it, which is a
               different sentence and belongs above the fields rather than
               beside one of them. #}
            {% if error is not null %}
                <div role="alert" class="flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3 text-sm text-danger">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <p class="leading-snug">{{ error }}</p>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        {% endblock %}

        {% block after_fields %}
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'settings.integrations.save_tests'|trans }}
            </p>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
